  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian Response to International Migrants in Transit through Honduras</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this IOM project is to contribute to dignified and decent living conditions for international migrants in transit, while promoting their autonomy and resilience. The project develops small renovation works and provides basic equipment in collective centers for international migrants in transit, provides safe transportation assistance and raises awareness on their rights and entitlements. Moreover, the project assists with conditional vouchers for rental, in-kind food assistance and NFI kits. The intervention provides humanitarian assistance to 25,817 people (12,052 men, 10,863 women and 2,902 children), including 850 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
